-- header-clashes/divergence --
suite: probes
case: header-clashes.tck
go: Go's newHeader reports extern func pp, whose C name P clashes with
  type P, at the func's name, not at the extern("P") C name it is about,
  and reports type char, a C keyword, naming no package and claiming no
  name for it.
why: The port reports the clash at the C name, and names char with its
  package and claims its name, decided by the language owner 2026-11-15.
same: none
-- header-clashes/exit --
1
-- header-clashes/stdout --
-- header-clashes/stderr --

