-- value-statements/divergence --
suite: emit-probes
case: value-statements.tck
go: Go's onlyValue leaves has out: has(m, k) written as a statement is not
  reported, and its backend lowers it to a call of a C function that
  does not exist, which does not compile. make(T, alloc) written as a
  statement, for a T that owns nothing, is not reported.
why: A builtin that only gives a value, written as a statement, is reported
  as not used, as len is: has, and make whose value owns nothing; has's
  value is dropped, as len's is, decided by the language owner
  2026-11-15. The C compiles and runs under the address, undefined
  behavior and leak sanitizers with clang -Wall -Werror.
same: none
-- value-statements/exit --
0
-- value-statements/stdout --
