suite: check-clean
case: examples/reflect-make
go: Go's checker takes make(T, alloc) written as a statement, for a T that
  owns nothing, for a call statement, and reports nothing; its C, which
  drops the value, is right.
why: make only gives a value, so the port reports it as not used, as len
  is, decided by the language owner 2026-11-15; the C is Go's, and only
  the warnings differ.
same: exit, stdout
