-- hdr-lib-test/divergence --
suite: test-examples
case: probe/c-uses-package-type
go: Go's tack.h, its types named by codegen/c's header.go cName, names a
  struct type of the program's last package by its Tack name alone, as
  it names package main's, where it gives any other package's type its
  package's name and an underscore first; the last package is main only
  in a program, so for a library, which --check loads, or a package
  loaded for its tests, Go's tack.h names that package's types otherwise
  than its own C, written against the names a program importing it
  gets, uses them.
why: The port gives a struct type its package's name and an underscore
  unless its package is named main, the names a program importing the
  package gets, so the package's C compiles against its tack.h, decided
  by the language owner 2026-11-18.
same: stdout
-- hdr-lib-test/exit --
0
-- hdr-lib-test/stdout --
-- hdr-lib-test/stderr --
ok test_fill
ok m/p: 1 test
