-- header-keyword-type-test/divergence --
suite: test-examples
case: probe/header-keyword-type
go: Go's tack.h names a struct type of the program's last package by its
  Tack name alone, so p's type auto, loaded for its tests or as a
  library, would be auto, a C keyword, which Go rejects.
why: The port names a struct type its package's name and an underscore
  unless its package is named main, so a package loaded for its tests or
  as a library is accepted and rejected exactly as a program importing
  it, decided by the language owner 2026-11-18, the accept and reject
  consequences accepted by the lead 2026-11-18.
same: stdout
-- header-keyword-type-test/exit --
0
-- header-keyword-type-test/stdout --
-- header-keyword-type-test/stderr --
ok test_fill
ok m/p: 1 test
