-- unicode18-lex/divergence --
suite: lex-probes
case: unicode18-string.tck
go: Go quotes a string's value in --lex's dump with strconv.Quote, whose
  unicode package is at Unicode 17.0.0, where U+0558 is unassigned, so
  it writes the rune as \u0558.
why: The port quotes with std/unicode, at Unicode 18.0.0, where U+0558
  is a letter and printable, so it writes the rune itself: the Unicode
  18.0.0 upgrade, owner ruling 2026-11-19, accepted as a divergence
  2026-11-19. The fuzz targets skip every input holding a rune the two
  versions classify apart (see skipUnicodeDrift).
same: exit, stderr
-- unicode18-lex/exit --
-- unicode18-lex/stdout --
[000:007] keyword(package)
[008:012] ident("main")
[012:012] ;
[014:229] comment("Strings of U+0558, a letter Unicode 18.0.0 assigns, written as itself\nand spelt by \\x escapes: the port quotes them in its --lex dump with\nstd/unicode, at 18.0.0, and Go with its unicode package, at 17.0.0.")
[230:233] keyword(var)
[234:235] ident("s")
[236:237] =
[238:242] string("՘")
[242:242] ;
[243:246] keyword(var)
[247:248] ident("t")
[249:250] =
[251:261] string("՘")
[261:261] ;
[262:262] EOF
-- unicode18-lex/stderr --
-- unicode18-printf-verb/divergence --
suite: probes
case: unicode18-printf-verb.tck
go: Go shows a printf verb that is not valid UTF-8 of graphic runes
  quoted, and its unicode package, at Unicode 17.0.0, has U+0558
  unassigned, so not graphic: it writes the verb as "%\u0558".
why: The port classifies with std/unicode, at Unicode 18.0.0, where
  U+0558 is a graphic letter, so it shows the verb as written, %՘:
  the Unicode 18.0.0 upgrade, owner ruling 2026-11-19, accepted as a
  divergence 2026-11-19 (see unicode18-lex).
same: exit, stdout
-- unicode18-printf-verb/exit --
-- unicode18-printf-verb/stdout --
