-- unicode18-switch-case/divergence --
suite: probes
case: unicode18-switch-case.tck
go: Go's checker names a duplicate string case by strconv.Quote of its
  value (typeck/switch.go's caseKeyOf), whose unicode package, at
  Unicode 17.0.0, has U+0558 unassigned, so it writes "\u0558".
why: The port quotes with std/conv and std/unicode, at Unicode 18.0.0,
  where U+0558 is a printable letter, so it writes the rune itself:
  the Unicode 18.0.0 upgrade, owner ruling 2026-11-19, which covers every
  place the compiler quotes or classifies a rune, diagnostic wording
  included (see unicode18-lex).
same: exit, stdout
